<section class="panel mb-4">
    <h3>Vendor authentication</h3>
    <p>Every retrieval and acknowledgment request requires an active vendor key in <code>X-API-Key</code>. Administrators generate keys under <strong>Administration → Vendors</strong>.</p>
    <p>The key identifies the vendor. <code>Vendor_Code</code> in the payload and <code>X-Vendor-Code</code> in the headers may be omitted; if supplied, each must match the key's vendor code. A mismatch or a category that is not permitted returns HTTP <code>403</code>. Invalid, expired, or revoked keys and inactive vendors return HTTP <code>401</code>.</p>
    <p>Institution access is configured per vendor as paired university and institution codes. A blank institution rule permits every institution within that university. Requests for an unauthorized university return <code>403</code>; within an authorized university, only permitted institutions appear in data, totals, pagination, incremental responses, and redeliveries. Codes ignore case and surrounding spaces, while leading zeros remain significant.</p>
    <p>After an access change, start a new full synchronization with <code>PageNo: 1</code>, an empty <code>lastUpdateDate</code>, and new idempotency keys. Previous-scope cursors and cached responses cannot continue under changed permissions; an existing idempotency key returns <code>409</code> when its scope changes. Acknowledging a delivery from a different scope returns <code>404</code>.</p>
    <p class="mb-0">Administrators can set key expiry dates and rotate with an overlap of up to 24 hours (1 hour by default). During overlap, both keys use the same vendor permissions, per-category rate limits, idempotency records, delivery history, and checkpoints. Switch to the current key before the previous key's cutoff. Responses identify the key as <code>current</code> or <code>previous</code> in <code>X-API-Key-Status</code>, and include <code>X-API-Key-Expires-At</code> as an ISO 8601 timestamp when a cutoff applies. Expiry is enforced on every request without a scheduled job.</p>
</section>
